---
// mboard data-model diagram: a surface-agnostic core, with the event log
// as the source of truth. Illustrates why the schema is "extensible".
---

<figure class="not-prose my-8 flex flex-col items-center">
  <div class="flex flex-col items-center">
    <span
      class="border-border bg-background text-muted-foreground rounded-full border px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium tracking-wide uppercase"
    >
      Surfaces — Slack today, Web UI later
    </span>
    <div class="border-border h-4 border-l border-dashed"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
    <span
      class="border-border bg-muted/40 text-foreground rounded-md border px-3 py-1.5 text-sm"
    >
      channel_links
    </span>
    <span class="text-muted-foreground text-xs">maps channel → board</span>
  </div>

  <div class="border-border h-4 border-l border-dashed"></div>

  <div
    class="border-accent/40 bg-muted/40 relative w-full max-w-md rounded-xl border p-5 pt-8"
  >
    <div class="absolute -top-3 left-4 flex items-center gap-2">
      <span
        class="bg-background text-accent px-2 text-xs font-medium tracking-wide uppercase"
      >
        Surface-agnostic core
      </span>
    </div>

    <ul class="text-foreground flex flex-col gap-2 text-sm">
      <li class="border-border bg-background rounded-md border px-2 py-1.5">
        <strong>boards</strong> — no Slack columns; the "Area" in the web UI
      </li>
      <li
        class="border-border bg-background flex flex-col gap-1 rounded-md border px-2 py-1.5"
      >
        <span><strong>tickets</strong> — built-in fields only</span>
        <span class="border-border ml-3 border-l pl-3 text-xs">
          ↳ <strong>ticket_events</strong> — one row per user action
          <br />
          <span class="ml-4">
            ↳ <strong>event_field_changes</strong> — source of truth for
            custom-field values
          </span>
        </span>
      </li>
      <li class="border-border bg-background rounded-md border px-2 py-1.5">
        <strong>field_definitions</strong> — custom-field schema per board
        (types are data, not migrations)
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="border-border h-4 border-l border-dashed"></div>

  <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
    <span
      class="border-border bg-background text-foreground rounded-md border px-3 py-1.5 text-sm"
    >
      users
    </span>
    <span
      class="border-border bg-background text-foreground rounded-md border px-3 py-1.5 text-sm"
    >
      user_identities
    </span>
    <span class="text-muted-foreground text-xs">all FKs local</span>
  </div>

  <figcaption class="text-muted-foreground mt-4 text-center text-sm">
    The board doesn't know Slack exists. Slack is just a row in
    <code>channel_links</code>; identity is indirected through
    <code>users</code>; and every custom-field value is derived from the event
    log. That's what "extensible" bought me — the web UI was an additive
    surface, not a rewrite.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
